FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] tests/bench_test.rs:432 — `edge_size_limit_boundary_is_exact_per_workload` runs every workload at its `max_size` inside the normal `cargo test --all-targets` gate: concat 100_000, lex 250_000, primes 10_000. Each call gets only the hard 60 s `DEFAULT_BUDGET` (tests/bench/mod.rs:31) and panics on `BudgetExceeded` (line 432-434). `concat` is O(n²) string copying (`Value::Text(format!("{}{}", a, b))` at src/runtime.rs:213) over 100k interpreter iterations, so the test's pass/fail depends on the gate machine's speed; a slower runner turns a correctness test into a spurious timeout failure. It also violates the phase's own separation that measurement stays outside the gate (Cargo.toml comment: "a measurement that writes `BENCH.md` must not run inside the test gate"). Fix: pin the maximum with `check_size_supported` (which does not run the workload, as `mod.rs`'s `edge_the_size_limit_is_enforced_without_running_the_workload` already does) and run one small, bounded size end-to-end. What would settle it: the measured wall time of this test on the gate machine; if it is a few seconds, downgrade.

2. [MINOR] tests/bench_test.rs:297 — `edge_a_hung_child_process_is_killed_at_its_budget` asserts a wall-clock bound (`since_started < child_sleep`, 500 ms budget vs 1500 ms sleep) and then sleeps only 1400 ms before checking the finish marker (line 317), leaving a 400 ms margin. The parent's timeout and the watcher's 2 ms polling are both subject to scheduling delay, so a loaded gate machine can return after the child's own sleep or fail the marker check — the exact flake class the phase says it avoids ("timing assertions are flakes wearing a gate's clothes"). Fix: make the child sleep much longer (e.g. 10 s), assert only that the process was killed (no finish marker after the parent returned), and drop the tight elapsed comparison.

3. [MINOR] tests/bench/mod.rs:1577 — `edge_child_measurement_accepts_an_explicit_environment` passes `&[]` for `env`, so it cannot fail if `measure_in_child` ignored its `env` argument entirely. The test name and the REPORT's claim ("accepts an explicit environment without mutating the process-global one") are not actually pinned by this test; the non-empty env path is only exercised incidentally by the hang test. Fix: pass a non-empty, observable environment entry through a hidden workload/marker and assert the child saw it (or drop the overclaiming test name/REPORT line).

4. [MINOR] tests/bench_test.rs:352 — `edge_bench_md_path_is_the_working_directory` silently skips all of its assertions whenever `RB_BENCH_OUTPUT` is set (`if std::env::var_os("RB_BENCH_OUTPUT").is_none()`). A test that an ambient environment variable can make inert is the environment-coupling the phase claims to have fixed; the deterministic helper (`bench_md_path_from`) is already covered in `mod.rs`. Fix: delete this test and rely on the direct helper test, or drive the env with an injected accessor.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 4
